      "notes": "PRIMARY (5-session return): per-date Spearman IC of each feature with the next-5-session return, tested in its declared direction (Newey-West, h_steps 5); pass per feature: signed IC mean > 0 with t >= 2.5; Benjamini-Hochberg at 5% across the 6 features (Bonferroni beside it; across the two horizons Bonferroni applies for any headline). SIGNS declared before the run, all -1 (higher feature, lower next return): downside demand (put-call IV spread, risk reversal, put/call open interest and its change) prices or predicts weakness; a steeper term slope is calm that mean-reverts (stress premium sits at inverted slopes); heavy option activity relative to open interest marks informed trading that leans bearish (Johnson-So)."
